<title>UK: Rolls-Royce, IAE win Korean aero engine deal.</title>
<headline>Rolls-Royce, IAE win Korean aero engine deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rolls-Royce Plc and its International Aero Engines partners have won a contract to supply V2500 engines to Korean short-haul carrier Asiana for its new fleet of 18 Airbus Industrie A321 airliners.  </p>
<p>Earlier this week Asiana, up to now an operator of aircraft powered by General Electric /CFM engines, said it would order 12 of the A321s, with options for a further six options.</p>
<p>International Aero Engines is a partnership of Rolls, United Technologies unit Pratt &amp; Whitney, Germany's MTU, a unit of Daimler Benz, and the  Japanese Aero Engines Corporation.</p>
<p>It has programme sales of around $12 billion.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
